From a13c872bcf13d16c7a7bf4b8ec3394a338f1f5e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: godpow <17231911+godpow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:06:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] texture_cache: Count what host images really take

The collector's memory total counted each image at its guest size: a
trimmed image (reduce_texture_resolution) at four times what it takes,
an unbacked one in full though it takes nothing. In Mario Kart World
the total sat over the critical limit for whole races, and the
collector evicted and re-created thousands of textures every 10
seconds, re-uploading them.

Images now count their host image's memory requirements where the
runtime reports them (Vulkan; none while unbacked), recorded at
registration so unregistering takes off the same amount. The texture
cache's periodic breakdown reports the same sizes.

On upstream: the host size goes through upstream's ImageMemoryBytes
instead of a size recorded at registration.

