From c1bf4c4833335389445ef751c466cc85905cc503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: godpow <17231911+godpow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:31:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] vulkan: Give staging buffers back sooner

The staging pool visited one of its 64 size classes a frame and freed
16 buffers there at most: the buffers a burst of uploads made, loading
a course in Mario Kart World, stayed for many seconds, on a phone
whose GPU memory is its RAM. Of 4.8 GB of Vulkan memory at its fourth
course, textures took 1.1 GB and buffers 1 GB.

Every size class is trimmed every frame now: a few idle buffers of each
size are kept for reuse (one of 16 MiB or more), and the rest go once
the GPU is done with them and they sat unused for 64 submissions. The
texture cache's periodic statistics report the pool's size.

