Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:26:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/18] vulkan: Keep no idle staging buffers of 16 MiB or more

e6f27d4b5d kept one idle staging buffer of each size of 16 MiB or more
for reuse. Sizes are powers of two, so one large image's upload made a
1 or 2 GiB buffer, and keeping one of each such size held the upload
pool at 4 GiB for the rest of the session: on the Odin 3, Mario Kart
World's Vulkan memory reached 10 GB a few courses in (6.2-7 GB before).

Large buffers now go once the GPU is done with them and they sat
unused for 64 submissions; up to four idle small ones are kept.

