From b174d1a77c958fc00d731170244581aea531167a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: godpow <17231911+godpow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:34:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] vulkan: back large texture arrays on phones instead of
 leaving them black

Mario Kart World's terrain textures are 8192x8192x68 arrays. On a GPU
that samples ASTC natively (Adreno) the ASTC ones never took the
per-layer sparse path, which was only for GPU-decoded ASTC, and stayed
unbacked: all zeros, dark surfaces. The BC6H one got 4 of 68 layers
under the 384 MiB cap.

- ASTC sampled natively uploads layer by layer like other plain formats.
- On mobile GPUs (memory is the system's RAM) one sparse image may bind
  1.5 GiB with 16 GiB of RAM or more, and images are trimmed to that,
  so a whole array fits (BC6H at mip 1+, ~1.45 GB).
- An image there that cannot be sparse is backed whole when it fits
  (or replaced once written, if its memory is still unwritten), rather
  than stay unbacked.

On upstream: kept next to the SparseTiles path; MakeImage takes
back_huge after upstream's aliased.

