From 8541be51d1b1bdff917cdb2b35598e919f4c7cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: godpow <17231911+godpow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:19:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] Add two settings that save memory for Switch 2 titles

Loading a Mario Kart World race takes its process to 19-20 GB, and a
24 GiB phone kills it. Both settings are off by default, switchable per
game, and listed with the renderer hacks on Android.

reduce_texture_resolution: a large compressed 2D texture (ASTC or BCn,
1024 pixels and up, with mip levels, at most 6 layers) keeps its levels
from 1 on, a quarter of the video memory. This uses the existing
TrimmedLevels support. Compressed formats are never render targets or
storage images. GPU copies by guest level are kept off trimmed images
(IsSafeGpuCopy, and AccelerateDMA falls back to copying through guest
memory), so they upload the levels they keep from there.

release_gpu_only_memory (experimental): Switch 2 textures in GPU-only
memory were kept twice, in the guest's RAM and in host images. Once an
image the host keeps byte for byte as the guest does is uploaded from
there, it is marked GPU modified, so reads through the caches and
eviction download it back first. Its guest backing is then given back
to the system: HostMemory::ReleaseBackingRegion punches holes in the
memfd, through DeviceMemoryManager::ReleaseMemory. Guest memory read
without going through the caches can see zeros there.

On upstream: releases through upstream's device_memory_ptr, before
upstream's cold hint (released memory is GPU modified and not hinted).

