From a4961d1456e4e7e8c88fec881c0e526571a3e4e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: godpow <17231911+godpow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:24:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] texture_cache: release_gpu_only_memory covers whole
 GPU-only regions

The setting only looked at images in sparse regions, and those are
mostly the terrain arrays it skips: it released next to nothing. The
regions nx2:gpu backs whole (7 GB in Mario Kart World, textures and
render targets) are now tracked for the texture cache too
(Nx2InGpuOnlyRegion), and images uploaded from them give back their
guest memory.

Images with trimmed host levels (reduce_texture_resolution) give back
only the guest levels the host doesn't keep, most of their bytes:
nothing reads those, and the levels the image keeps stay in guest
memory to upload again after an eviction. Other images are released
whole and marked GPU modified as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (implementation and debugging)
(cherry picked from commit 587fe1fb9ba4965f748ed04e3b726cc1d8b72c5b)
---
 src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h               |  2 ++
 src/video_core/nx2.h                         | 25 +++++++++++++++
 src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h | 33 ++++++++++++++------
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h b/src/core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h
